shura.cpp: sources and licenses

shura.cpp 1.0 is released under the MIT License. It is llama.cpp v1.0.0 with the parts of Shura that upstream does not have,
added where possible on top of upstream's own mechanisms. It combines code from these sources, all under the MIT License:

1. llama.cpp (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp)
   Copyright (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors. The upstream LICENSE and AUTHORS files are kept unchanged. The base of shura.cpp 1.0
   is the tag v1.0.0. The MoE expert cache (src/llama-moe-cache.cpp, its graph and scheduler parts, docs/moe-cache.md and
   scripts/moe-cache-tune.py) is upstream's; shura.cpp adds live resize, an empty state and statistics to it.

2. thecodacus/llama.cpp, branch `perf` (https://github.com/thecodacus/llama.cpp), by Anirban Kar
   The starting point of the earlier versions of this fork (up to the `shura` branch). Its MoE expert cache, scheduler prefetch,
   tools/moe-trace and qwen4exp conversion are in the history of those versions; they are not part of the 1.0 tree unless a part
   is listed in docs/SHURA.md as brought back.

3. TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant, branch `feature/turboquant-kv-cache` (https://github.com/TheTom/llama-cpp-turboquant)
   The TurboQuant KV cache types of the earlier versions. In 1.0 they are present only if docs/SHURA.md says so.

4. Changes written for Shura, Copyright (c) 2026 hikkian
   The VRAM governor and its endpoints, pause with a checkpoint and resume, live resize of the expert cache with rollback, the
   pinned memory limit, the abort check of the CUDA/HIP backend, the reasoning-budget extensions (THINK3b), the diagnostics and
   the tests for them, listed in docs/SHURA.md.

Model weights are not part of this repository and are covered by their own licenses.
